{"chunk_id": "dataset_desc_mu::c004", "document_id": "dataset_desc_mu", "sequence": 4, "source_start": 812, "source_end": 1335, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Station Distribution\n\nThe 847 stations are distributed across 48 states (excluding Alaska and Hawaii). States with the highest station density include California (94 stations), Texas (78 stations), and New York (52 stations). Stations are categorized into three types: urban (412 stations, 48.6%), rural (301 stations, 35.5%), and remote (134 stations, 15.8%). The mean elevation of stations is 342 meters above sea level, with a range from 2 meters (Key West, FL) to 3,214 meters (Mauna Loa Observatory, HI proxy station).", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 523, "source_document_hash": "97ae7a648bafcc06dda856fa36ea474b4d621b13b01a651710c3a5d47d51a6c4", "structure": {"section_ids": ["dataset_desc_mu#s1"], "paragraph_ids": ["dataset_desc_mu#s1#p1"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
